        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive secure software verification and testing specification aligned with the NIST SP 800-218 Secure Software Development Framework, specifically addressing the PW.8 practice area. The spec should define our end-to-end testing lifecycle: scoping criteria for what gets tested (including all third-party executable code and reusable in-house modules), test design methodology selection based on software maturity stage, execution procedures covering both static and dynamic analysis, and a documentation standard for results. It must require robust functional testing of all security features, mandate integration of dynamic vulnerability scanning into our CI/CD automated test suites, and establish a regression testing protocol that incorporates tests for all previously reported vulnerabilities so defects aren't reintroduced. All discovered issues and recommended remediations must be recorded and triaged within our Jira-based workflow tracking system. The specification should also require that test environments replicate production infrastructure stacks and technology configurations as closely as feasible, including sandboxed execution environments for untrusted code. Please map all requirements back to the relevant SSDF practices, reference applicable NIST SP 800-53 SA-11 controls, IEC 62443 SVV verification levels, and EO 14028 Section 4e obligations. We'd like a draft ready for architecture review by end of next sprint.",
